From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:11:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vh265: skip the buffer level gate once input has ended

run_ready waits for pre_decode_buf_level bytes before every run. When
input ends with less than that left, nothing more can arrive. The
decoder stops short of the data it holds and never reports empty, so
the last pictures never show. vdec_ready_to_run already skips its own
level checks under input.eos.
---
 drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
@@ -0,7 +0,8 @@
 			(int)(get_jiffies_64() - hevc->sc_start_time) * 1000/HZ);
 	}
 	if (vdec_stream_based(vdec)
-			&& pre_decode_buf_level != 0) {
+			&& pre_decode_buf_level != 0
+			&& !vdec->input.eos) {
 			u32 rp, wp, level;
 
 			rp = STBUF_READ(&vdec->vbuf, get_rp);
